From 8364637f42475dd0604c240bafce17964ddd149d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 07:02:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] hc-mix: Q8_0 mixer path - persistent down counters,
 planar output, Q8_1 epilogue, combine+norm fusion

Fewer launches per hc site for models whose hc weights are Q8_0/F32 (unsloth
UD quants), bit-identical to the current Q8_0 path, BF16 path unchanged:
- down_dots counters: per-stream zero-once buffer, the finisher resets its
  counter; no memset per call (GGML_CUDA_HC_DONE_PERSIST=0: off)
- planar mixed/inject output, no ggml_cont on the verify band
  (LLAMA_HC_MIX_PLANAR_Q8=0: off)
- Q8_1 of the mixed rows written by the collapse kernel into the quantize
  cache, quantize_q8_1 arithmetic incl. d*int-sum (GGML_CUDA_HC_Q8_EPI=0: off)
- HC_COMBINE + norm + Q8_1 in one kernel, hc_mix_combine_rms_gamma_q8
  (GGML_CUDA_FUSE_HC_COMBINE_MIX_Q8=0: off)

